# AI agent commands (canonical)

When the user sends one of these **exact intents**, follow the linked workflow — do not guess or implement unrelated work.

| Command | Meaning | Required actions |
|---------|---------|------------------|
| **Update?** | Status snapshot only | Refresh `plan/mission-control-master-tasks.md`; run narrow CI/checks; report done / next / blocked. **Do not implement features.** |
| **next** | Implement top priority task | Read **Recommended next queue** → linked GitHub issue → `procedure-init` if multi-file → implement → test → update registry. |
| **sync issues** | Refresh GitHub board | `npm run sync:labels` → `npm run sync:tasks` → `npm run setup:github-project` |
| **sync tasks** | Same as sync issues | Alias for board sync |
| **autopilot** | Merge-ready PR | Per `.cursor/rules/procedure-github-project.mdc` autopilot section |
| **procedure** | Start tracked work | `node scripts/procedure-init.mjs --title "…"` |

## Priority order for **next**

1. P0 issues (`priority:p0` / Project Priority P0) — e.g. AUTH-13
2. P1 queue in `procedure/github-milestones.json`
3. First `next` row in master registry not blocked

## Files agents must read

| Command context | Read first |
|-----------------|------------|
| Any Mission Control work | `MISSION-CONTROL-WALKTHROUGH.md`, `plan/mission-control-master-tasks.md` |
| GitHub Issues / Project | `TASK-TRACKING.md`, `docs/guides/GITHUB_ISSUES_AND_PROJECT.md` |
| Ecosystem roadmap | `docs/wiki/Ecosystem-Roadmap.md` |

## Data hygiene (AI conversations)

- Do **not** paste secrets, tokens, vault passphrases, or full `.env` in chat
- Use cred vault (`cred get cursor <key>`) — mask previews only
- Before destructive ops (deploy, delete, mass close issues), use `confirmAction` / ask user
- Track procedure file **Progress** — not full chat logs

